  "body": "@jensimmons and I were looking at the rendering of PICTURE, and, it seems like the default display type of `inline` isn't quite ideal. [testcase](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?%3Cpicture%20style%3D%22border%3A%20double%20orange%3B%22%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Csource%20srcset%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fplacehold.it%2F80x80%22%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20media%3D%22(min-width%3A%20800px)%22%3E%0A%20%20%20%20%3Cimg%20src%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fplacehold.it%2F90x90%22%20%2F%3E%0A%3C%2Fpicture%3E)\r\n\r\nIf the PICTURE element is swapped in place of a raw IMG, then the rendering changes significantly because the PICTURE is just an inline box, and does not have an aspect ratio or anything like that. It might be useful to add `display: contents` here, so that PICTURE effectively has the behavior of representing a replaced element, rather than the behavior of representing a replaced element inside a SPAN.",
